-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ח/4 — הסכמים קיבוציים שנחתמו עם ארגון המורים העל-יסודיים ב-24.1.2008
-- The implementing instructions for the 24.1.2008 agreements with the
-- secondary teachers' organisation: stage A of the reform (an individual
-- teaching hour for a 4.5% supplement, 8.5% from 1.1.2009), the 4% erosion
-- update of the salary table and the shekel supplements, and the public-
-- sector supplement of 1.5% / 3% / 5% — all paid from February 2008's salary.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `הסכמים קיבוציים עם ארגון המורים העל-יסודיים, 24.1.2008`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, subject line, and the recital that these are the instructions for the agreements signed on 24.1.2008 with the State, the Centre of Local Government and the three large cities; no rule.

-- Time in this file is counted in salary months from January 2008 (1):
-- February 2008 is 2, December 2008 is 12, January 2009 is 13, December
-- 2009 is 24.
`January 2008`  MEANS 1
`February 2008` MEANS 2
`March 2008`    MEANS 3
`April 2008`    MEANS 4
`June 2008`     MEANS 6
`December 2008` MEANS 12
`January 2009`  MEANS 13
`December 2009` MEANS 24

DECLARE `employer action` IS ONE OF
    `show the supplement on its own payslip line`
    `make up January's individual hours`
    `deduct for individual hours not done` HAS `hours deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the January 2008 supplements and differences` HAS `amount paid` IS A NUMBER

@desc A teaching employee as far as this circular asks about them.
DECLARE `secondary teacher` HAS
    `in secondary education under an owning body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed by the employers in secondary education, at an owning body
    `graded as a teaching employee`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc on the teaching-employees' salary grading
    `represented by the teachers' organisation`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc represented by ארגון המורים
    `is a school principal`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `position percent`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc the position held at this owning body, in percent (100 = a full position)
    `combined salary`                             IS A NUMBER  @desc השכר המשולב for the month; an input
    `supplement 94`                               IS A NUMBER  @desc תוספת '94 for the month; an input
    `supplement 2001`                             IS A NUMBER  @desc תוספת 2001 for the month; an input
    `public-sector supplement`                    IS A NUMBER  @desc the supplement of section 4 ("תוספת 2008") for the month
    `does the individual hours`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc does the individual-teaching hours (or, for a principal, the additional work hour) the circular requires of them

§§ `1 תחולה`

@ref akn:art_1/p1
GIVEN t IS A `secondary teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement applies to` t IF
        t's `in secondary education under an owning body`
    AND t's `graded as a teaching employee`
    AND t's `represented by the teachers' organisation`

§§ `2 יישום שלב א' ברפורמה`

-- §2א: the stage-A supplement, out of the 26% agreed for the reform: 4.5%
-- from 1.1.2008 (paid with February's salary, back to January) for one
-- weekly individual hour; from 1.1.2009 4% more, 8.5% in all, for two. Its
-- base is the combined salary, תוספת '94, תוספת 2001 and "תוספת 2008 (see
-- section 4 above)" — §4's supplement, printed below and not above.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_a/p2
GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the stage-A rate` month IS
    BRANCH IF month AT LEAST `January 2009` THEN 8.5%
           IF month AT LEAST `January 2008` THEN 4.5%
           OTHERWISE 0

`the reform's agreed total` MEANS 26%

GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly individual hours of a full position` month IS
    IF month AT LEAST `January 2009` THEN 2 ELSE 1

GIVEN t IS A `secondary teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the stage-A base` t IS
    t's `combined salary`
    PLUS t's `supplement 94`
    PLUS t's `supplement 2001`
    PLUS t's `public-sector supplement`

-- §2ב: by the position fraction, up to 100% at the same owning body. (The
-- sentence is printed twice over in the corpus text.)
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN t IS A `secondary teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position share` t IS
    min (t's `position percent` DIVIDED BY 100) 1

§§ `2ה Positions under 90%`

-- §2ה: the duty of individual hours for positions under 90%.
DECLARE `period unit` IS ONE OF `a week`, `a month`

DECLARE `individual-hours duty` HAS
    `duty hours` IS A NUMBER
    `duty per`   IS A `period unit`

@desc A row of §2ה's table: a band of position percent and the individual hours it owes from 1.1.2008 and from 1.1.2009.
DECLARE `part-time band` HAS
    `band lowest percent`  IS A NUMBER
    `band highest percent` IS A NUMBER
    `duty from 1.1.2008`   IS AN `individual-hours duty`
    `duty from 1.1.2009`   IS AN `individual-hours duty`

-- The table AS PRINTED (positions in whole percent, as the bands are).
-- ¶4, ¶6 and ¶8 are the word "בחודש" (a month) of the cells above them.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e akn:art_2__para_e/p2 akn:art_2__para_e/p3 akn:art_2__para_e/p4 akn:art_2__para_e/p5 akn:art_2__para_e/p6 akn:art_2__para_e/p7 akn:art_2__para_e/p8
`the part-time table` MEANS
    LIST `part-time band` 75 89 (`individual-hours duty` 3 `a month`) (`individual-hours duty` 6 `a month`),
         `part-time band` 50 74 (`individual-hours duty` 2 `a month`) (`individual-hours duty` 1 `a week`),
         `part-time band` 25 49 (`individual-hours duty` 1 `a month`) (`individual-hours duty` 2 `a month`)

`the full-position floor` MEANS 90

GIVEN pct IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `part-time band`
DECIDE `the bands the table gives for` pct IS
    filter (GIVEN b YIELD pct AT LEAST b's `band lowest percent` AND pct AT MOST b's `band highest percent`)
           `the part-time table`

-- The reading adopted (F-2007-08_tashsach_04-a): a band runs up to the next
-- band's lowest percent ([75, 90), [50, 75), [25, 50)), and a position under
-- 25% owes what the lowest row sets.
GIVEN pct IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `individual-hours duty`
DECIDE `the individual-hours duty` pct month IS
    IF pct AT LEAST `the full-position floor`
    THEN `individual-hours duty` (`weekly individual hours of a full position` month) `a week`
    ELSE IF month AT LEAST `January 2009`
         THEN BRANCH IF pct AT LEAST 75 THEN `individual-hours duty` 6 `a month`
                     IF pct AT LEAST 50 THEN `individual-hours duty` 1 `a week`
                     OTHERWISE `individual-hours duty` 2 `a month`
         ELSE BRANCH IF pct AT LEAST 75 THEN `individual-hours duty` 3 `a month`
                     IF pct AT LEAST 50 THEN `individual-hours duty` 2 `a month`
                     OTHERWISE `individual-hours duty` 1 `a month`

-- §2ו–ח: an individual hour is work with a group of one to five pupils,
-- as the principal decides in coordination with the teacher; it is in the
-- teacher's work plan; and it does not change the position fraction.
@ref akn:art_2__para_f akn:art_2__para_g
@desc One hour offered as an individual hour.
DECLARE `individual hour` HAS
    `pupils in the group`                     IS A NUMBER
    `set by the principal with the teacher`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the teacher's work plan`             IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS AN `individual hour`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as an individual hour` h IF
        h's `pupils in the group` AT LEAST 1
    AND h's `pupils in the group` AT MOST 5
    AND h's `set by the principal with the teacher`
    AND h's `in the teacher's work plan`

@ref akn:art_2__para_h
GIVEN t IS A `secondary teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position percent with the individual hour` t IS
    t's `position percent`

-- §2ט: §2א–ז apply to principals, who instead of the individual teaching
-- hour work an additional hour beyond their position, as the Ministry
-- directs.
@ref akn:art_2__para_i
DECLARE `the hour owed` IS ONE OF
    `an individual teaching hour`
    `an additional work hour beyond the position`

GIVEN t IS A `secondary teacher`
GIVETH AN `the hour owed`
DECIDE `the kind of hour owed` t IS
    IF t's `is a school principal`
    THEN `an additional work hour beyond the position`
    ELSE `an individual teaching hour`

-- §2י: after six months (after June 2008's salary) the supplement goes on
-- only if the parties have reached a comprehensive secondary reform by then;
-- otherwise it stops, and the individual hour with it.
@ref akn:art_2__para_j
GIVEN month IS A NUMBER, `comprehensive reform agreed by June 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stage A runs in` month `comprehensive reform agreed by June 2008` IF
        month AT LEAST `January 2008`
    AND (month AT MOST `June 2008` OR `comprehensive reform agreed by June 2008`)

§§ `2 The stage-A supplement in all`

-- §2א's rate on its base, by §2ב's position share, for a teacher §1 covers
-- who does the hours §2ה–ט require, while §2י lets stage A run.
@export The stage-A reform supplement a secondary teacher is owed for one salary month under circular 2007-08/4
GIVEN t IS A `secondary teacher` @desc the teacher and the month's salary components
      month IS A NUMBER @desc the salary month, January 2008 = 1
      `comprehensive reform agreed by June 2008` IS A BOOLEAN @desc whether the parties reached the comprehensive reform by June 2008 (section 2י)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the stage-A supplement` t month `comprehensive reform agreed by June 2008` IS
    IF `the agreement applies to` t
       AND t's `does the individual hours`
       AND `stage A runs in` month `comprehensive reform agreed by June 2008`
    THEN `the stage-A rate` month TIMES `the stage-A base` t TIMES `the position share` t
    ELSE 0

§§ `2ג–ד What the stage-A supplement counts in`

-- §2ג–ד and §4.1ג–ד: what each supplement is counted in.
DECLARE `purpose` IS ONE OF
    `percentage supplements on the combined salary`
    `supplement 2001 itself`
    `the hour value`
    `severance pay`
    `pension and pension contributions`
    `continuing-education and Dafna funds and other deductions on the combined salary`
    `the minimum-wage top-up`

@ref akn:art_2__para_c akn:art_2__para_d
GIVEN p IS A `purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stage-A supplement counts in` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `percentage supplements on the combined salary` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `pension and pension contributions` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- §2ג ¶2 and §4.1ב: each supplement is shown on a separate payslip line.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c/p2 akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `employer action`
DECIDE `the supplements get their own payslip lines` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `show the supplement on its own payslip line`
    WITHIN `February 2008`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "sections 2ג and 4.1ב: each supplement is a separate line on the payslip"

-- §2ה's Ministry note: individual hours not done in January 2008 are made up
-- in February–March 2008; a teacher who does not is docked, with April
-- 2008's salary, for the hours not done — provided the employer let them do
-- them. F-2007-08_tashsach_04-b: the circular does not say what an hour is
-- docked at; the rate is an input.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e/p9 akn:art_2__para_e/p10 akn:art_2__para_e/p11 akn:art_2__para_e/p12
GIVEN `hours owed from January` IS A NUMBER, `the employer let them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `employer action`
DECIDE `January's individual hours` `hours owed from January` `the employer let them` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `make up January's individual hours`
    WITHIN `March 2008`
    LEST  IF `the employer let them`
          THEN PARTY `the employer`
               MUST  `deduct for individual hours not done` n
                     PROVIDED n EQUALS `hours owed from January`
               WITHIN `April 2008` MINUS `March 2008`
          ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `hours not done` IS A NUMBER, `rate docked per hour` IS A NUMBER, `the employer let them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the April 2008 deduction` `hours not done` `rate docked per hour` `the employer let them` IS
    IF `the employer let them` THEN `hours not done` TIMES `rate docked per hour` ELSE 0

-- akn:art_2__para_ja A pointer to the pedagogical annex at the end of the circular, encoded below.

§§ `3 תשלום בגין שחיקת השכר לשנים 2002–2007`

-- akn:art_3 The heading and the recital (¶1–4): the 1.2.2007 agreement sent the erosion dispute for 1.1.1999–31.12.2006 to arbitration, the award of 22.5.2007 covered 1.1.1999–31.12.2001, and the 24.1.2008 agreement set the erosion for 1.1.2002–31.12.2006 and 2007; no rule.

-- §3א: the combined-salary table rises 4% from 1.1.2008. The updated table
-- is "attached as annex A"; the corpus holds no annex A (only the
-- pedagogical annex), so the table is not data here.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a
`the erosion update` MEANS 4%

GIVEN `December 2007 table amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the combined-salary table from 1.1.2008` `December 2007 table amount` IS
    `December 2007 table amount` TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion update`)

-- §3ב: the shekel supplements 87 and 94 rise 4% from 1.1.2008, on their
-- December 2007 values.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_3
DECLARE `shekel supplement` IS ONE OF
    `supplement of agreement 87`
    `supplement of agreement 94, teaching reinforcement`

GIVEN s IS A `shekel supplement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `updated by the erosion 4%` s IF TRUE

GIVEN `December 2007 amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a shekel supplement from 1.1.2008, by the erosion update` `December 2007 amount` IS
    `December 2007 amount` TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion update`)

§§ `4 תוספת שכר במגזר הציבורי, 1.7.2005–31.12.2009`

-- §4.1א: the supplement on the combined salary and תוספת 2001, from the
-- salary of January 2008 1.5%, of December 2008 3%, of December 2009 5%.
-- §4.1ה: the shekel supplements rise at the same rates and dates.
@ref akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_a akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_a__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_a__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_a__cls_3 akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_e akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_e__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_e__cls_2
GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the public-sector rate` month IS
    BRANCH IF month AT LEAST `December 2009` THEN 5%
           IF month AT LEAST `December 2008` THEN 3%
           IF month AT LEAST `January 2008`  THEN 1.5%
           OTHERWISE 0

-- §4.1ו: both are computed on the components' December 2007 values.
@ref akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_f
GIVEN `December 2007 combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `December 2007 supplement 2001` IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the public-sector supplement for` `December 2007 combined salary` `December 2007 supplement 2001` month IS
    `the public-sector rate` month
    TIMES (`December 2007 combined salary` PLUS `December 2007 supplement 2001`)

-- Both updates (§3ב's 4% and §4.1ה's rate) are on the December 2007 value.
GIVEN `December 2007 amount` IS A NUMBER, month IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a shekel supplement in` `December 2007 amount` month IS
    `December 2007 amount`
    TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion update` PLUS `the public-sector rate` month)

-- §4.1ה.3's definition: "shekel supplements" are all the shekel supplements
-- of the teaching grading on the eve of the agreement, except those not
-- updated by cost-of-living agreements and the minimum-wage top-up. (Its
-- 5% step from December 2009 is in `the public-sector rate` above.)
@ref akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_e__cls_3
@desc A shekel supplement as section 4.1ה.3 asks about it.
DECLARE `a shekel payment` HAS
    `paid on the eve of the agreement`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `updated by cost-of-living agreements`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the minimum-wage top-up`                     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN s IS A `a shekel payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a shekel supplement under section 4` s IF
        s's `paid on the eve of the agreement`
    AND s's `updated by cost-of-living agreements`
    AND (NOT s's `is the minimum-wage top-up`)

-- §4.1ג–ד: the supplement is salary for every purpose — counted in the
-- percentage supplements on the combined salary (but not in תוספת 2001),
-- the hour value, severance, pensions and every contribution or deduction
-- usual on the combined salary — and not in the minimum-wage top-up.
@ref akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_c akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_d
GIVEN p IS A `purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the public-sector supplement counts in` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `supplement 2001 itself` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the minimum-wage top-up` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- §4.1ז: the amounts of supplements 87 and 94 after §3ב and this section, as
-- printed; read as their amounts from January 2008 (the 1.5% step).
@ref akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_g akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_g__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_1__subpara_g__cls_2
GIVEN s IS A `shekel supplement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the printed amount from January 2008` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `supplement of agreement 87` THEN 158.80
    WHEN `supplement of agreement 94, teaching reinforcement` THEN 142.79

-- §4 ¶1–2: everything is paid with February 2008's salary, January's
-- differences with it.
@ref akn:art_4/p1 akn:art_4/p2
GIVEN `January's amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `employer action`
DECIDE `paid with February 2008's salary` `January's amount` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the January 2008 supplements and differences` x
          PROVIDED x AT LEAST `January's amount`
    WITHIN `February 2008`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 4: the payments and January's differences are made with February 2008's salary"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and the two signatures; no rule.

§§ `נספח פדגוגי — השעה הפרטנית`

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 The annex's addressee (school principals), greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- ¶4: every teacher owes one individual hour a week, with a group of one to
-- five pupils, for a 4.5% supplement (F-2007-08_tashsach_04-c).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p4
`the annex's weekly hours for every teacher` MEANS 1
`the annex's rate` MEANS 4.5%

-- ¶5–9: the suggested uses.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8 akn:att_1__hc_1/p9
DECLARE `suggested use` IS ONE OF
    `dialogue and a personal bond with the pupils`
    `learning reinforcement: support, deepening and broadening`
    `work with challenging pupils`
    `guiding pupils' research projects`

-- ¶10–21: the operating principles, as conditions on how a school arranges
-- the hour.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p10 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 akn:att_1__hc_1/p12 akn:att_1__hc_1/p13 akn:att_1__hc_1/p14 akn:att_1__hc_1/p15 akn:att_1__hc_1/p16 akn:att_1__hc_1/p17 akn:att_1__hc_1/p18 akn:att_1__hc_1/p19 akn:att_1__hc_1/p20 akn:att_1__hc_1/p21
@desc How a school has arranged the individual hours.
DECLARE `school arrangement` HAS
    `a fixed slot in the personal and school timetable`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `largest group taught`                              IS A NUMBER
    `groups formed by principal and teachers from the pupils' mapping` IS A BOOLEAN
    `groups flexible through the year`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `every teacher assigned to a group`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported and assessed in pedagogical meetings`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `outside class lessons, at day's end or in windows` IS A BOOLEAN
    `plan coordinated with the class teacher`           IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS A `school arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `follows the annex's principles` a IF
        a's `a fixed slot in the personal and school timetable`
    AND a's `largest group taught` AT MOST 5
    AND a's `groups formed by principal and teachers from the pupils' mapping`
    AND a's `groups flexible through the year`
    AND a's `every teacher assigned to a group`
    AND a's `reported and assessed in pedagogical meetings`
    AND a's `outside class lessons, at day's end or in windows`
    AND a's `plan coordinated with the class teacher`

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p22 akn:att_1__hc_1/p23 akn:att_1__hc_1/p24 The annex's sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_04-a: §2ה's bands leave positions with no row — any
-- position under 25%, and any between two bands' printed bounds.
`the part-time table leaves positions without a row` MEANS
        null (`the bands the table gives for` 20)
    AND null (`the bands the table gives for` 89.5)
    AND null (`the bands the table gives for` 74.5)
    AND null (`the bands the table gives for` 49.5)
#ASSERT `the part-time table leaves positions without a row`

-- Every whole percent from 25 to 89 has exactly one row.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD count (`the bands the table gives for` n) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST 25, 30, 49, 50, 60, 74, 75, 80, 89)

-- The adopted reading agrees with the table wherever the table has a row.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN b YIELD `the individual-hours duty` (b's `band lowest percent`) `January 2008` EQUALS b's `duty from 1.1.2008`
                       AND `the individual-hours duty` (b's `band highest percent`) `January 2009` EQUALS b's `duty from 1.1.2009`)
            `the part-time table`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_04-b: the deduction for individual hours not done
-- names no rate; the two rates the circular itself mentions differ.
`the April deduction depends on a rate the circular does not set` MEANS
    NOT (`the April 2008 deduction` 2 50 TRUE EQUALS `the April 2008 deduction` 2 80 TRUE)
#ASSERT `the April deduction depends on a rate the circular does not set`

-- F-2007-08_tashsach_04-c: the annex tells principals every teacher owes
-- one individual hour a week; §2ה sets a half-position teacher's 2008 duty
-- at two hours a month.
`the annex and §2ה differ for a half position` MEANS
    NOT (`the individual-hours duty` 50 `January 2008`
         EQUALS `individual-hours duty` `the annex's weekly hours for every teacher` `a week`)
#ASSERT `the annex and §2ה differ for a half position`

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Every salary figure is a placeholder.
`a full-time secondary teacher` MEANS
    `secondary teacher` WITH
        `in secondary education under an owning body` IS TRUE
        `graded as a teaching employee`               IS TRUE
        `represented by the teachers' organisation`   IS TRUE
        `is a school principal`                       IS FALSE
        `position percent`                            IS 100
        `combined salary`                             IS 8000
        `supplement 94`                               IS 500
        `supplement 2001`                             IS 1000
        `public-sector supplement`                    IS 500
        `does the individual hours`                   IS TRUE

`a principal on a 120% position` MEANS
    `secondary teacher` WITH
        `in secondary education under an owning body` IS TRUE
        `graded as a teaching employee`               IS TRUE
        `represented by the teachers' organisation`   IS TRUE
        `is a school principal`                       IS TRUE
        `position percent`                            IS 120
        `combined salary`                             IS 8000
        `supplement 94`                               IS 500
        `supplement 2001`                             IS 1000
        `public-sector supplement`                    IS 500
        `does the individual hours`                   IS TRUE

-- 4.5% of 10,000 = 450; 8.5% from January 2009 = 850 if the reform was
-- agreed, 0 if not; the 120% position is capped at 100%.
#ASSERT `the stage-A supplement` `a full-time secondary teacher` `February 2008` FALSE EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `the stage-A supplement` `a full-time secondary teacher` `January 2009` TRUE EQUALS 850
#ASSERT `the stage-A supplement` `a full-time secondary teacher` `January 2009` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the stage-A supplement` `a principal on a 120% position` `February 2008` FALSE EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `the kind of hour owed` `a principal on a 120% position` EQUALS `an additional work hour beyond the position`
#ASSERT `the stage-A rate` `January 2009` MINUS `the stage-A rate` `December 2008` EQUALS 4%
#ASSERT `the public-sector supplement for` 8000 1000 `June 2008` EQUALS 135
#ASSERT `the public-sector supplement for` 8000 1000 `December 2009` EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `a shekel supplement in` 100 `January 2008` EQUALS 105.5
#ASSERT `a shekel supplement from 1.1.2008, by the erosion update` 100 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT NOT `the stage-A supplement counts in` `the hour value`
#ASSERT `the public-sector supplement counts in` `the hour value`
